A rougelike game I play called POWDER deals with intrinsics in this
manner, and I think it works out very well. Eating corpses can confer
all sorts of intrinsics (mostly good, some bad), but only temporarily.
This makes rings and artifacts more valuble as you try and gain as
much permanent resistance as you can without having to rely on
corpses, making some tougher equipment choices and rewarding the
preparedness and apadability. The game has a spell for preserving
corpses, much akin to Nethack's tinning kit, so you can save useful
snacks for later when you really need a specific resistance, so with
the help of a tinning kit in Nethack you can be sure to have
resistances when you really need them.

I'm not sure how easy it would be to balance into Nethack, but I'd
suggest looking at POWDER for a good example of that mechanic being
implemented.



